Enginehost: a window icon the game does not ship is not a fatal error (Ren'Py 7.4 to 7.8).

set_icon loads config.window_icon the first time the display starts and only
a web download is caught, so a game whose icon file is missing stopped at the
main menu with IOError and then took the process down with SIGSEGV (rig
2026-10-16, BareWitness on the RP5: "Couldn't find file
'gui/BWLogoMenuWindow2.png'" at set_icon, Droidtop/tracker#411). A handheld
has no window icon to set; skip it, as the 8.x patch does.
--- a/renpy/display/core.py
+++ b/renpy/display/core.py
@@ -1168,6 +1168,9 @@
                 pygame.display.set_icon(im)
             except renpy.webloader.DownloadNeeded:
                 pass
+            except Exception as e:
+                # Enginehost: a missing or unreadable icon leaves the window without one.
+                renpy.display.log.write("Window icon %r not set: %r", icon, e)
 
     def set_window_caption(self, force=False):
 
